{"availability":"available","full":"jsakamoto/Toolbelt.Blazor.SpeechSynthesis","name":"Toolbelt.Blazor.SpeechSynthesis","description":"SpeechSynthesis API access for your Blazor apps.","category":"Developer tools","language":"C#","stars":98,"forks":19,"created":"2018-10-19T13:53:10Z","updated":"2026-01-31T06:33:33Z","license":"MPL-2.0","branch":"master","homepage":"https://jsakamoto.github.io/Toolbelt.Blazor.SpeechSynthesis/","topics":["blazor","speech-synthesis"],"demo":"https://jsakamoto.github.io/Toolbelt.Blazor.SpeechSynthesis/","color":"#63362a","ink":"#f8c7a8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-20T01:48:45.029Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-20T01:48:45.029Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-20T01:48:45.029Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-05T21:33:22.351Z","stars":98,"forks":19},{"at":"2026-10-08T00:28:54.631Z","stars":98,"forks":19},{"at":"2026-10-10T05:41:17.844Z","stars":98,"forks":19},{"at":"2026-10-15T18:02:00.336Z","stars":98,"forks":19},{"at":"2026-10-19T18:02:36.536Z","stars":98,"forks":19},{"at":"2026-10-20T01:48:45.029Z","stars":98,"forks":19}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["This is a class library for Blazor app (both \"WebAssembly App\" client-side model and \"Server App\" server-side model) to provide Speech Synthesis API access.","We know that .NET 9 or later allows us to use import maps to import JavaScript files with a fingerprint in their file names. Therefore, in .NET 9 or later Blazor apps, you may want to avoid appending a version query string to the JavaScript file URL that this library loads.","However, we recommend keeping the default behavior of appending a version query string to the JavaScript file URL. The reason is that published Blazor WebAssembly standalone apps don't include import map entries for JavaScript files from NuGet packages. This inconsistent behavior between development and production environments and hosting models may lead to unexpected issues that are hard to diagnose, particularly in AutoRender mod